WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.030
On the 7th of January, Orthodox churches
in Russia and Serbia celebrate Christmas.

2
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:11.150
In 2026, Western churches keep
Easter on the 5th of April.

3
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.210
Most Orthodox churches
wait until the 12th.

4
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.390
Same faith.

5
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:16.740
The same Creed.

6
00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.150
Different days.

7
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.600
So why do some Christians
keep Christmas on 7 January,

8
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.390
and Easter weeks after their neighbours?

9
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.790
In this mission, you'll see
how the Council of Nicaea,

10
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:32.660
in 325, wanted every church to
keep Easter on the same Sunday.

11
00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:35.980
Then you'll compare how East
and West keep Christmas night,

12
00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:37.890
and the night of Easter.

13
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.870
Your mission: find out why Christians
who share one faith keep these feasts on

14
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.040
different days.
